      counterexample: PG(2,5)+C7@0+C7@1  v=7  ecc(v)=5  rad=4  (no neighbour descends)
      counterexample: PG(2,5)+C7@0+C7@1  v=8  ecc(v)=5  rad=4  (no neighbour descends)
      counterexample: PG(2,5)+C7@0+C7@1  v=9  ecc(v)=5  rad=4  (no neighbour descends)
      counterexample: PG(2,5)+C7@0+C7@1  v=10  ecc(v)=5  rad=4  (no neighbour descends)
      VERDICT: (L1) IS FALSE AS STATED.  Eccentricity has non-global local minima.
      E14 used it to derive 'ecc(w) >= 2*rad'.  That derivation is INVALID.

