      first witness: dense(s=1,n0=14) n=12 w=0 rad=2 ecc(w)=3 2*rad=4 a(w)=3
      VERDICT: (L2) IS FALSE INSIDE THIS LINE'S CLASS TOO.

  (L3) E14's BONUS LOCAL LEMMA (rad=2, C4-free => N(w) = {a}, so a(w)=1).
      ITS PROOF IS INVALID AS WRITTEN: it exhibits w-a-c-m-n-w and calls it a
      4-cycle.  Those are FIVE distinct vertices -- w,a,c,m,n -- so it is a C5 and
