PART 4 -- THE SINGLE-HAIR RESIDUAL CLASS, LOCATED IN VERTICES, AND WHETHER THE
          ROUND-38 COST RULE ALREADY COVERS IT
==============================================================================
Draft 42.4's single-hair table leaves exactly one open row:
    h = 1,  e := ecc_{G'}(w) = rad(G')+1,  rad(G'+pendant) = rad(G')+1.
By (RAD-1P) the third conjunct IS 'w maximally far from every centre of G''.
So the residual class is  R(G,w) := [ ecc(w) = rad+1 ]  AND  [ w rad-extremal ].
What that row needs is exactly  endpath(G,w) >= ecc(w)+3  -- the (TAIL-2) step.

DIRECTION OF ERROR, FIXED BEFORE THE NUMBERS: a residual vertex is COVERED only by
BUILDING an induced anchored path on ecc(w)+3 vertices and passing the independent
checker.  So COVERED is a LOWER bound and UNCOVERED an UPPER bound.

