PART 5 -- (CS-3) AGAINST E14's FAMILY: absolute vs relative thresholds
==============================================================================
(CS-3), draft 45/ r36 sec.5: G connected C4-free, delta >= 2, r = rad >= 3.  If some
vertex is maximally far from every centre then |C| <= n - 1 - delta(delta-1) - (r-3).

   k    n  delta  rad  |Ctr|  (CS-3) bound  |Ctr| <= bound  |Ctr|/n
    1   13      2    3      2            10  True           0.154
    2   16      2    3      3            13  True           0.188
    4   22      2    3      5            19  True           0.227
    8   34      2    3      9            31  True           0.265
   16   58      2    3     17            55  True           0.293
   32  106      2    3     33           103  True           0.311

  READING, and it is the harvest's real content: E14's family does NOT contradict
  (CS-3).  It refutes only the ABSOLUTE form of the r34 target ('|Ctr| large' with a
  universal constant), which (CS-3) never asserted.  |Ctr|/n -> 1/3 while the bound
  stays far above it, because delta = 2 makes delta(delta-1) = 2 and the bound nearly
  vacuous.  So the harvest CONFIRMS that (CS-3)'s dependence on n and delta is
  NECESSARY, not an artefact of how it was proved.

  WHERE (CS-3) ACTUALLY BITES, measured over this line's own host family:
    hosts in scope (rad >= 3): 365;  hosts where (CS-3) DECIDES (|C| > bound): 175
    every deciding host re-checked by BFS: no radius-extremal vertex found.

