PART 6 -- E39 HARVEST (out/ox-alpha/E39_w133_multihair_caseII_out.md), UNREAD until
          this round.  Verdict PARTIAL, two theorems, one 'universal' lemma.
==============================================================================
E39's LEMMA 0: path(G') <= 2*rad(G')+1, with the proof 'd(a,b) >= d_P(a,b) = p-1'.
THE PROOF IS INVALID: an INDUCED path is an induced SUBGRAPH; its endpoints may be
far closer in G than along it.  d(a,b) <= p-1 is what holds, and the proof needs the
reverse.  Whether the STATEMENT survives is a separate question, so it is measured:

   host              n  rad  path(G)  2*rad+1  Lemma 0 holds
   C6                6    3        5        7  True
   C7                7    3        6        7  True
   C9                9    4        8        9  True
   Theta(3,3,3)      8    3        6        7  True
   Petersen         10    2        5        5  True
   P5                5    2        5        5  True
   C5+C5 glued       9    2        7        5  False
   PG(2,3)          26    3       11        7  False

  VERDICT: E39's LEMMA 0 IS FALSE, on 2 of 8 hosts tested.  Widest gap: PG(2,3),
  rad = 3, so the lemma allows 7 vertices and the graph carries 11 -- over by 4.
  (PRE-REGISTERED PREDICTION THAT FAILED, recorded: I expected Petersen to be the
  witness at path = 6.  MEASURED path(Petersen) = 5, so Lemma 0 HOLDS there.  The
  refutation came from hosts I added for coverage, not from the one I named.)
  CONSEQUENCE, and it is the whole point of reading this output: Lemma 0 is the LAST
  STEP of Theorem P1 ('path(G) >= 2 rad(G) >= (2r'+1)+Delta >= path(G')+Delta') and
  of Theorem P2.  BOTH THEOREMS FALL WITH IT.  Nothing of E39 sec.3 may be cited.
  E39's sec.1 verification of the (MH-II) => Case-II chain is a separate matter and
  is NOT touched by this -- that part re-derives, and I re-derived it by hand.

  E39's 'LEMMA X FALSE' WITNESS, rebuilt from its own edge list:
    n=5  connected=True  C4-free=True  mu=1  rad=2  centre=['z', 'a', 'b']
    THE WITNESS IS C4-FREE AS CLAIMED, AND IT HAS mu = 1 < 2.
    w and u are pendants, so a(w) = a(u) = 1.  E39's 'blocker' is therefore not
    known to block anything inside this line's class -- the obstruction it names
    lives on a graph route A2 never has to handle.  Not a refutation of E39's
    honesty (it says PARTIAL); a statement about what the PARTIAL is about.

